<title identifier="/us/usc/t10"><num value="10">Title 10—</num><heading>ARMED FORCES</heading>
<subtitle identifier="/us/usc/t10/stA"><num value="A">Subtitle A—</num><heading>General Military Law</heading>
<part identifier="/us/usc/t10/stA/ptII"><num value="II">PART II—</num><heading>PERSONNEL</heading>
<chapter identifier="/us/usc/t10/stA/ptII/ch55"><num value="55">CHAPTER 55—</num><heading>MEDICAL AND DENTAL CARE</heading>
<section style="-uslm-lc:I80" id="id888361fb-76cd-11f0-8437-f8ad163dc8c2" identifier="/us/usc/t10/s1074c"><num value="1074c">§ 1074c.</num><heading> Medical care: authority to provide a wig</heading><content>
<p style="-uslm-lc:I11" class="indent0">A person entitled to medical care under this chapter who has alopecia resulting from the treatment of a malignant disease may be furnished a wig if the person has not previously been furnished one at the expense of the United States.</p>
</content><sourceCredit id="id888361fc-76cd-11f0-8437-f8ad163dc8c2">(Added <ref href="/us/pl/98/525/tXIV/s1401/e/2/A">Pub. L. 98–525, title XIV, § 1401(e)(2)(A)</ref>, <date date="1984-10-19">Oct. 19, 1984</date>, <ref href="/us/stat/98/2616">98 Stat. 2616</ref>, § 1074b; renumbered § 1074c, <ref href="/us/pl/102/190/dA/tVI/s640/a/1">Pub. L. 102–190, div. A, title VI, § 640(a)(1)</ref>, <date date="1991-12-05">Dec. 5, 1991</date>, <ref href="/us/stat/105/1385">105 Stat. 1385</ref>.)</sourceCredit>
<notes type="uscNote" id="id888361fd-76cd-11f0-8437-f8ad163dc8c2">
